    <mxCell id="caption" value="Dots are recorded cells from evals/results/trend-data.json; feature lines are three-version rolling means, refusal and quality lines are raw; the x-axis is ordinal, only measured versions appear. A hollow dot is a lower bound (part of its spend went unrecorded); a dashed vertical rule is a change of the requested root model; the dashed reliability line is the known-defect clear rate, a rolling mean. Method and definitions: evals/README.md § Reading the figure; every score: evals/results/TREND.md." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#9AA5B1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="940" width="700" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
